{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/52098-hindu-and-muslim-compacts-conspiracies","id":52098,"title":"hindu and muslim compacts/conspiracies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-17T20:02:03-08:00","id":52098,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> hindu and muslim compacts/conspiracies?","content":"I am wondering what sort of compacts and/or conspiracies might exist for either the Hindu or Muslim Faiths? I am not sure if any are for them within the books, so I am wondering if others might have ideas for them? <br /> <br /> -herkles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T21:38:14-08:00","id":52130,"title":"","content":"Well first off the Ascending Ones is largely based out of North Africa, the Middle East, and Central Asia - and incorporate heretical mysticisms of Abrahamic faiths. They are in many ways based on the MYTHIC hashashins/assassins. Based on myths and occultism they obviously don't fit accurate religious doctrine and practices of Islam (not that they're exclusively Muslim, they're not, their roots are lot older); but hypocrisy and darkness (in this case the drugs) are kind of a built in feature at Tier 3 (notice that Malleus Maleficarum are by definition heretical witches, for example).<br /> <br /> In a VtR book &quot;Ancient Bloodlines&quot; a Hunter Compact, Ahl al-Jabal is covered, which is actually based on the HISTORIC Crusades era Naziri Ismailis. I'm not a huge fan of this write up for modern day usage because while the MYTHIC group (Ascending Ones) could survive as a secret conspiracy over the centuries, the actual historic group surviving as a secret society strains the realism its striving for. So while I would use the Ahl al-Jabal in a historic campaign, I wouldn't use them as is in a modern one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok some non-canon ideas<br /> <br /> Salat al-Layl (Night Prayer) is a Compact that is essentially the Muslim world's version of the Union (an archetypical type of Compact found in different cultures), dedicated to defending the Ummah. Obviously they have a more religious character than the Union, but that's natural in cultures that make less of a distinction between religious and social community. If I were to pick the type of Supernatural they have the most enmity toward, it would be Jahiliyyah cults and their false-gods (Arisen).<br /> <br /> Prarabdhavat (fruit bearing banyan tree) is a Conspiracy (though a small one - a &quot;your ability to wield this endowment makes you a member&quot; situation like the Lucifuge, rather than &quot;being a member lets you get this endowment&quot; like most others). Hindu hunters who have connected with past lives and deliver karma unto supernatural immortals who have wronged past selves, but whose undying nature means they would otherwise avoid karmic consequences for defying dharma.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And obviously if it needs to be said, Muslim and Hindu Hunters are welcome in pretty much any of the non-religious Hunter organizations (Task Force VALKYRIE, the Union, Null Mysteriis, Barrett Commission, VASCU, the Cheiron Group, Night Watch, Talbot Group.... Loyalists of Thule might be a tad tricky for a religious Muslim, but theosophy was heavily influenced by Hinduism, etc etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T21:48:11-08:00","id":52134,"title":"","content":"I know Ancient Bloodlines has Muslim Brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:35:54-08:00","id":52420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/52098-hindu-and-muslim-compacts-conspiracies?p=52130#post52130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first off the Ascending Ones is largely based out of North Africa, the Middle East, and Central Asia - and incorporate heretical mysticisms of Abrahamic faiths. They are in many ways based on the MYTHIC hashashins/assassins. Based on myths and occultism they obviously don't fit accurate religious doctrine and practices of Islam (not that they're exclusively Muslim, they're not, their roots are lot older); but hypocrisy and darkness (in this case the drugs) are kind of a built in feature at Tier 3 (notice that Malleus Maleficarum are by definition heretical witches, for example).<br /> <br /> In a VtR book &quot;Ancient Bloodlines&quot; a Hunter Compact, Ahl al-Jabal is covered, which is actually based on the HISTORIC Crusades era Naziri Ismailis. I'm not a huge fan of this write up for modern day usage because while the MYTHIC group (Ascending Ones) could survive as a secret conspiracy over the centuries, the actual historic group surviving as a secret society strains the realism its striving for. So while I would use the Ahl al-Jabal in a historic campaign, I wouldn't use them as is in a modern one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I was aware of the ascending ones though it felt like they were more alchemists though. I was not aware of the Ahl-al-Jabal though, I might take a look at them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/52098-hindu-and-muslim-compacts-conspiracies?p=52130#post52130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok some non-canon ideas<br /> <br /> Salat al-Layl (Night Prayer) is a Compact that is essentially the Muslim world's version of the Union (an archetypical type of Compact found in different cultures), dedicated to defending the Ummah. Obviously they have a more religious character than the Union, but that's natural in cultures that make less of a distinction between religious and social community. If I were to pick the type of Supernatural they have the most enmity toward, it would be Jahiliyyah cults and their false-gods (Arisen).<br /> <br /> Prarabdhavat (fruit bearing banyan tree) is a Conspiracy (though a small one - a &quot;your ability to wield this endowment makes you a member&quot; situation like the Lucifuge, rather than &quot;being a member lets you get this endowment&quot; like most others). Hindu hunters who have connected with past lives and deliver karma unto supernatural immortals who have wronged past selves, but whose undying nature means they would otherwise avoid karmic consequences for defying dharma.</div> </div> </div> </div>interesting ideas, those are cool. Though, I wonder if there are any more conspicy ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}